('78', 'The Cenotaph War Memorial', 'Penang', 'The Cenotaph, also known as Penang War Memorial, is a cenotaph located at the Esplanade in George Town, Penang, Malaysia. The site of the Cenopath is situated at the shoreline of the Esplanade, at Jalan Tun Syed Sheh Barakbah (at a section of street also known as The Esplanade) and Jalan Padang Kota Lama (Esplanade Road), by the padang (open field) and the City Hall that it fronts.The present Cenotaph is a 1948 reconstruction of the original built in 1929.', 'The Cenotaph War Memorial, Esplanade Sea Wall Heritage Trail, Central George Town, 10910 George Town, Penang, Malaysia', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/GEORGETOWN_PENANG_ISLAND_MALAYSIA_JAN_2012_%286815563818%29.jpg/400px-GEORGETOWN_PENANG_ISLAND_MALAYSIA_JAN_2012_%286815563818%29.jpg', '2026-08-11 22:35:38', '2026-08-12 00:04:45'),
('79', 'World Peace Memorial', 'Penang', 'The World Peace Memorial is in the form of an embossed pillar, with the words World Peace in English & Chinese text, topped with a sculpture featuring a flock of Doves in flight.', 'World Peace Memorial, Ayer Itam Road, Farlim, 11060 George Town, Penang, Malaysia', NULL, '2026-08-11 22:35:38', '2026-08-11 22:35:38'),
('80', 'Padang Brown', 'Penang', NULL, 'Brown Memorial, Perak Road, Central George Town, 10450 George Town, Penang, Malaysia', NULL, '2026-08-11 22:35:39', '2026-08-11 22:35:39'),
